    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>2022 WHO classification of conjunctival melanocytic intraepithelial lesions (C-MILs)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Raymond L. Barnhill",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-table-layout-alt: fixed; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.8pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>WHO classification</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.75pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Acceptable alternative terminology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Increased cellularity</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.75pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histological features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.1pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Risk of association with or progression to invasive melanoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>n/a</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Benign melanosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">C-MIN (grades&nbsp;0&ndash;1)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">PAM without atypia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">No/minimal</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Conjunctival hypermelanosis (increased pigment in epithelial cells without melanocytic hyperplasia or atypia)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Slight or focal melanocytic hyperplasia without atypia (parabasal melanocytes with condensed round nuclei, smaller than basal epithelial cell, inconspicuous nucleoli, and inconspicuous cytoplasm) may be seen</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">None</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Low-grade C-MIL</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">PAM with mild atypia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">C-MIN (grades&nbsp;2&ndash;4)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Yes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Predominantly basilar melanocytic proliferation with low-grade atypia (dendritic or small to moderate-sized polyhedral, usually non-epithelioid melanocytes with round to irregular nuclear contours, often nuclear hyperchromasia, inconspicuous nucleoli, and inconspicuous or scant cytoplasm)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lower</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>High-grade C-MIL</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">PAM with moderate to severe atypia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">C-MIN (grade&nbsp;5&ndash;10)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Yes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">More confluent basilar and significant non-basilar proliferation of melanocytes with high-grade atypia (moderate to severe), evidence of intraepithelial nested and/or pagetoid growth, and epithelioid cell cytomorphology</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Higher</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Melanoma in&nbsp;situ</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 70.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"95\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Yes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 304.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"406\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">The term &ldquo;melanoma in&nbsp;situ&rdquo; may be used for (1)&nbsp;the most atypical high-grade C-MILs involving close to the full thickness of the epithelium, (2)&nbsp;histologically obvious melanomas without documented evidence of subepithelial invasion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 122.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"163\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Highest</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">C-MIN, conjunctival melanocytic intraepithelial neoplasia; n/a, not applicable; PAM, primary acquired melanosis.</p>",
